# Build context for the canary box images (integration-suite/local/Dockerfile.*),
# whose context is the REPO ROOT because they bake the checkout in.
#
# Until those images existed no build had a repo-root context — the sandbox image
# builds from integration-suite/, the runner from integration-suite/local/ — so a
# stray file in the tree could never reach a layer. That changes here, and these
# images are PUBLIC on GHCR, so this file is the boundary.
#
# THE CANARY WRITES REAL CREDENTIALS INTO ITS CHECKOUT AT RUN TIME. ci-entrypoint.sh
# decodes the vendor OAuth tarballs and assembles the gateway env-file, and both
# used to land under the repo root. They are moved to a run-scoped directory in
# this same change, and they are ALSO named here: a cleanup trap that does not run
# (a killed run, a `docker kill`) is the normal case, not the exotic one, and
# `install.sh --build-local` builds from the operator's own checkout — which on the
# box is the very tree those files land in.
#
# The Dockerfiles additionally ASSERT none of these arrived, so a rename here that
# silently stops matching fails the build instead of publishing a credential.

# ── credentials and per-run state (see above) ───────────────────────────────
tokens/
tokens-*/
canary.env
canary-*.env
integration-suite-state*.json
secrets.env
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── rebuilt inside the image, or irrelevant to it ───────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
out/
coverage/
target/
*.tgz
*.log

# ── local scratch that has no business in a published image ─────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store

# The SHA is passed as a build ARG instead — baking 100+ MB of history to run
# `git rev-parse` once is not a trade. translate reconstitutes the one commit it
# needs at run time (it has to reach the remote to push anyway).
.git/
